{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1430697-optimal-sphere-selection","id":1430697,"title":"Optimal Sphere selection","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-01-01T16:24:08-08:00","id":1430697,"title":"Optimal Sphere selection","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> For starting characters with Arete 3, I did the math for future costs of spheres, and the less expensive option is to start with two spheres at 3, however, it might be useful to have low ratings but broad capabilities.<br /> <br /> That being said, what is better to have:<ul><li><i>Two spheres at 3 dots:</i><br /> I was thinking Mind 3 (easy to keep coincidental, broadly applicable) and Entropy 3 (easy to keep coincidental, broadly applicable).</li> <li><i>One sphere at 3, and three at 1:</i><br /> My picks would be Entropy 1, Life 3, Mind 1, Prime 1.</li> </ul><br /> What option do you think is best, and what would be your sphere picks in both scenarios?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 01-01-2021, 07:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-01T17:07:02-08:00","id":1430699,"title":"","content":"Spirit 3 mostly.. because you can seriously cheat with it. Talens are your friends.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Prime 3 would be honorable mention for raw utility if you are using Wonder sphere rules then you are functionally gadgeteer/D&amp;D wizard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2715,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","user":"Lian","date":". 01-01-2021, 08:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-01T17:29:55-08:00","id":1430704,"title":"","content":"In terms of cost, I'm curious how 3/3 compares to 3/2/1 where the 1 is your favored Sphere to maximize your (scant) XP discount.<br /> <br /> 3/2/1 also opens up a bunch of options for concepts compared to 3/3 or 3/1/1/1.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-01T18:00:17-08:00","id":1430706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1430697-optimal-sphere-selection?p=1430704#post1430704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In terms of cost, I'm curious how 3/3 compares to 3/2/1 where the 1 is your favored Sphere to maximize your (scant) XP discount.<br /> <br /> 3/2/1 also opens up a bunch of options for concepts compared to 3/3 or 3/1/1/1.</div> </div> </div> </div>The calculation is assuming you want to have 6 spheres at the same rating in the end, all them at 3, 4, or 5 dots, it doesn't matter as longs as the six end up in the same value. Adding more spheres is a flat cost, doesn't modify the end result.<br /> <br /> All calculations had the favoured sphere at the lowest possible value when several options are possible.<br /> <br /> Less expensive to more expensive: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>3/3</b></li> <li><b>3/1/1/1</b> (<i>One experience point over the first option).</i></li> <li><b>3/2/1</b> (<i>Three experience points over the first option).</i></li> <li><b>1/1/1/1/1/1</b> (<i>Five experience points over the first option).</i></li> <li><b>2/1/1/1/1</b> (<i>Seven experience points over the first option).</i></li> <li><b>2/2/1/1</b> (<i>Nine experience points over the first option).</i></li> <li><b>2/2/2</b> (<i>Twelve experience points over the first option).</i></li> </ol><br /> It is not that much of a difference but it adds up.<br /> <br /> That is in cost, but also there is the price to be paid in versatility: a mage with six 1's has a lot of extra senses, but next to nothing in capabilities to do new things. A mage with two 3's is limited to those 2 sphere effects, but is quite potent at them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 01-03-2021, 04:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-01T18:00:38-08:00","id":1430707,"title":"","content":"How useful 3/3 would be depends on the character's Focus per M20 terms and how much the Storyteller will allow. Entropy 3 and Mind 3 will give a lot of options, but Mind will be limited against any supernatural since it's at Willpower+3 and they can probably resist with one of their Nightfolk power. Entropy 3 might move probability and allow destruction of material objects, but then you're depending on skills for other uses.<br /> <br /> It's hard to know how high the spheres need to be, so for comparison, let's consider getting 4 spheres to three.<br /> 3/1/1/1 would require a minimum of 69 XP to raise to 3 across the board (one of the spheres at 1 is a specialty sphere, so it's 7 or 8 points to get each sphere at 1 to 2 and then 14 or 16 points to get each sphere at 2 to 3).<br /> <br /> 3/2/1 would require the addition of one of the 4 spheres after character creation. The cost to raise would be 79 XP if the sphere at 1 is the specialty sphere (since you have to have a dot in a specialty sphere). If there were two dots in the specialty sphere, that's 72 XP (34 XP to buy the new sphere and get it to rank 3 and 14 to raise the rank 2 to a 3 and 24 to raise the rank 1 to a 3).<br /> <br /> You can take 3/3 at character generation if you have the Arete, since a starting PC has six spheres. So, 3/1/1/1 is a little cheaper than 3/2/1 if you want to get 4 different spheres to rank 3. However, you'd be trading some flexibility later for doing rank 3/rank 2 combo effects out of the gate.<br /> <br /> Since Prime 2 can be used in creation, I'd rather have 3/2/1 at start with the following spheres: Pattern Sphere at 3 (Forces, Life, or Matter and Spirit if you think it's a Pattern sphere) Mind 1 (multitasking for additional actions and mental boosts) and Prime 2 (for creating Charms and creating things in the pattern).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-01T18:21:48-08:00","id":1430710,"title":"","content":"Sphere &amp; Focus picks greatly depend on what do you want to be able to do.<br /> <br /> Let's remember also that in Ascencion, unlike Awakening, multi-Sphere rotes are the norm, not the exception. Having two spheres a 3 can lock you out not only of the other Spheres, but also of some uses of your own maxed Spheres","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-01T18:35:56-08:00","id":1430712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1430697-optimal-sphere-selection?p=1430704#post1430704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In terms of cost, I'm curious how 3/3 compares to 3/2/1 where the 1 is your favored Sphere to maximize your (scant) XP discount.<br /> <br /> 3/2/1 also opens up a bunch of options for concepts compared to 3/3 or 3/1/1/1.</div> </div> </div> </div> I've always said Forces 3, Prime 2, Mind 1 is the vampire hunter's starter pack; physical invisibility, fireballs, and mind shields (oh my).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-02T10:26:51-08:00","id":1430759,"title":"","content":"Would it be worth buying up to Arete 3 even if you don't intend on bumping your spheres that high at character creation? For example, if I was going to make an Alchemist in an efficient way, I'm assuming you would want Life, Matter and perhaps Forces, so let's put 2 in each. If you wanted to get to the point where you could turn skin to steel, blood to acid, etc would that 8 FP investment be better so you could spread the relatively cheap FP around in backgrounds, abilities, etc be good or do you feel it is best to have a sphere at 3 if you are going to buy Arete that high?<br /> <br /> I hope that isn't confusing or stupid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26575-anarchorawlsian","name":"anarchorawlsian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-02T10:36:31-08:00","id":1430760,"title":"","content":"Arete 3 gives you 3 dice to roll in your casting pool. It's also the <i>only</i> source of dice for your casting pool. That alone makes it worth taking. <br /> <br /> If you want your Alchemist to make magical potions, you'll want Prime, too. Off the top of my head, I'm not recalling how many dots; I <i>think</i> it's 2 to make Charms (batches on one-use Wonders), though it might be 3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-02T11:52:47-08:00","id":1430771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I <i>think</i> it's 2 to make Charms (batches on one-use Wonders), though it might be 3.</div> </div> </div> </div>2 with Tass that has an appropriate resonance, 3 otherwise","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-02T16:11:36-08:00","id":1430801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1430697-optimal-sphere-selection?p=1430699#post1430699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Prime 3 would be honorable mention for raw utility if you are using Wonder sphere rules then you are functionally gadgeteer/D&amp;D wizard.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1430697-optimal-sphere-selection?p=1430771#post1430771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 2 with Tass that has an appropriate resonance, 3 otherwise</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not understand the fascination with Wonder creation for an starting character, if I read the book right: &quot;<i>In order to craft a wonder, the character must have all of the necessary Spheres</i>.&quot;, so what good is being able to craft it without many other spheres to create something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-02T17:27:24-08:00","id":1430810,"title":"","content":"I'm going with Prime 2 because then I can thrown Fireballs if I go with Forces, make stuff with Matter, create simple Life with Prime and so forth. If I go Life 3 Prime 2, I can make healing potions and better body potions. Charms in a batch could be quite useful, even for low levels. Just being able to see Forces or Life or Spirit can allow a lot of detection possibilities. Entropy 2/Prime 2 you can make luck items and hand them out. . .<br /> <br /> However, the utility of Prime varies greatly on how much Quintessence is available in the chronicle. If Quintessence is rare, then making a Wonder is less important than if Quintessence is readily available. The same is true for Spirit based on how hard it is to safely enter the Umbra (hence why I use the Avatar Storm as existing but not a constant danger).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-02T18:17:19-08:00","id":1430814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1430697-optimal-sphere-selection?p=1430801#post1430801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not understand the fascination with Wonder creation for an starting character, if I read the book right: &quot;<i>In order to craft a wonder, the character must have all of the necessary Spheres</i>.&quot;, so what good is being able to craft it without many other spheres to create something?</div> </div> </div> </div>The biggest thing is that a lot of effects are rated lower if you're using them on yourself.<br /> <br /> So, if you're making a character that focuses on healing, you can heal others directly with Life 3, or make healing Charms with Life 2/Prime 2; though they have to be activated by the injured party.<br /> <br /> Those healing Charms are lower in difficulty to make, and can be made ahead of time to take advantage of ritual casting and so on.<br /> <br /> Mage isn't that different from other RPGs where having healing spells is good, but having healing spells and lots of healing potions is even better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-03T01:16:23-08:00","id":1430844,"title":"","content":"Note that Prime 2/3 it's also the easiest way to get Agg damage by enhancing weapons. And it makes Qintessence gathering a lot easier. And it's also required for many powerful rotes, like the <a href=\"https://denvermage.fandom.com/wiki/Rotes_-_Traditions#Gift_of_Prana\" target=\"_blank\">Gift of Prana</a>.<br /> <br /> However, it's true that Prime's utility greatly depends on its synergy with other Spheres. It's not that great by itself.<br /> Still a solid choice to have from the start, as it helps all things magick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 01-03-2021, 04:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-03T08:55:07-08:00","id":1430874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1430697-optimal-sphere-selection?p=1430710#post1430710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sphere &amp; Focus picks greatly depend on what do you want to be able to do.<br /> <br /> Let's remember also that in Ascencion, unlike Awakening, multi-Sphere rotes are the norm, not the exception. Having two spheres a 3 can lock you out not only of the other Spheres, but also of some uses of your own maxed Spheres</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the answer. I was thinking something about the lines of:<ul><li>Paradigm: <i>Everything is Data</i></li> <li>Practices: <i>Psionics</i></li> <li>Instruments: <i>symbols; writings, inscriptions, and runes; languages, eye contact, energy, thought forms, meditation</i></li> </ul><br /> The character believes that reality is a simulation and understands that simulated computers inside the false reality would not be effective to alter the simulation itself (a disagreement with the Virtual Adepts), only privileged users of the system with the right permissions can alter reality; therefore everything should be &quot;mental&quot; magic, sending orders to the simulation while being aware of the true nature of reality, close to how <i>The Matrix</i> justifies Neo's abilities in the first movie.<br /> <br /> For a reality-is-just-information based character Entropy 3 + Mind 3 seemed adequate, and she would be able to do all the things both spheres offer (except those that require conjunctional effects).<br /> <br /> I was planning to have the character do a lot of information gathering that seemed like crazy intuitive for someone else, but for her, it is just listing permissions. I was using Contessa's powers in <i>Worm </i>as an inspiration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 01-03-2021, 02:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-03T09:34:09-08:00","id":1430878,"title":"","content":"To me, Correspondence is the Sphere of mathematics. Its spatial aspects are a reflection of mathematics-as-geometry/topology/etc., while its connection to the Digital Web derives from the equally intimate relationship between mathematics and information science. (And in my World of Darkness, what most people think of as the Digital Web is just the tip of the iceberg: beyond the Formatted Nodes lies a wide expanse of reality that has traditionally been thought of as part of the Astral Umbra, such as Platonic Reality where mathematical notions have a manifest existence.)<br /> <br /> If it were me, I'd definitely take a couple of dots of Correspondence for that concept.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, you should still choose a seventh Instrument, even though you've already discarded it. The reason is that you can still choose to use it, and you get a -1 difficulty modifier on the Arete roll of you do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 01-03-2021, 12:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-03T09:53:12-08:00","id":1430882,"title":"","content":"Not to mention that it's *the* sphere for information gathering. Otherwise you can only get whatever intel it's near you","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-03T10:12:23-08:00","id":1430884,"title":"","content":"Put another way: in the context of the Practice of Psionics, it's <i>the</i> Sphere for Clairvoyance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-03T11:36:19-08:00","id":1430896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1430697-optimal-sphere-selection?p=1430878#post1430878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me, Correspondence is the Sphere of mathematics. Its spatial aspects are a reflection of mathematics-as-geometry/topology/etc., while its connection to the Digital Web derives from the equally intimate relationship between mathematics and information science. (And in my World of Darkness, what most people think of as the Digital Web is just the tip of the iceberg: beyond the Formatted Nodes lies a wide expanse of reality that has traditionally been thought of as part of the Astral Umbra, such as Platonic Reality where mathematical notions have a manifest existence.)<br /> <br /> If it were me, I'd definitely take a couple of dots of Correspondence for that concept.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, you should still choose a seventh Instrument, even though you've already discarded it. The reason is that you can still choose to use it, and you get a -1 difficulty modifier on the Arete roll of you do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the instrument information, I have updated the post, can you please reference the page and book for M20?<br /> <br /> And regarding the original question what sphere dot combination: 3/3, 3/2/1, or 3/1/1/1 ? And which spheres?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 01-03-2021, 02:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-03T12:14:26-08:00","id":1430899,"title":"","content":"I'm working right now, so I don't have time to look things up; but check the list of Magickal Modifiers: you'll find one that says something to the effect of \u201cusing an instrument that you've surpassed: -1 difficulty\u201d. <br /> <br /> As for the Spheres, that's obviously up to you. But keep in mind that Correspondence 3 is when it shifts from \u201cClairvoyance\u201d to \u201cTeleportation\u201d. <br /> <br /> Another possibility would be Mind 3, Correspondence 2, and a dot in something else in preparation for later development. Forces 1, for example, isn't enough for Psychokinesis on its own; but it means that you only need one more for before you can start doing things that <i>would</i> qualify as PK. <br /> <br /> You might consider Life 1, as that's one of the few Spheres that does not than just enhance your senses: IIRC, Life 1 lets you enhance your physical attributes, giving you the option to be stronger, tougher, and/or faster as needed. That <i>can</i> be fit into Psionics (biokinesis is a thing); but it's more of a stretch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-03T12:31:09-08:00","id":1430902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1430697-optimal-sphere-selection?p=1430899#post1430899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You might consider Life 1, as that's one of the few Spheres that does not than just enhance your senses: IIRC, Life 1 lets you enhance your physical attributes, giving you the option to be stronger, tougher, and/or faster as needed. That <i>can</i> be fit into Psionics (biokinesis is a thing); but it's more of a stretch.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the answer.<br /> <br /> It is Life 3 what boosts attributes, as per <i>M20 How Do You Do That</i>:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Rank 3 Life</b> Arts (Rank 4 for other characters) <b>can boost<br /> or lower body-based Attributes by one dot per success</b> rolled.<br /> <b>Altered Physical and Social Attributes generally reveal themselves</b><br /> in obvious ways: rippling muscles, beautiful features, straighter<br /> posture, rapid reflexes, and so forth. <b>Mental Attributes might<br /> be increased the same way</b>, either by <b>altering the character\u2019s<br /> sensory organs (raising Perception) or his brain matter and<br /> capacity (raising Intelligence or Wits)</b>. </div> </div> </div>So for certain boosting effects Life can supplement Mind. And in the same book is stated that those attributes can be made permanent at half the experience cost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 01-03-2021, 03:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-03T12:43:44-08:00","id":1430904,"title":"","content":"Hrm. I may have been getting my Ascension and Awakening mixed up.<br /> <br /> If you're willing to give up that third dot of Mind, you might try something like Mind 2/Correspondence 2/Forces 2 to do a psi who is telepathic, clairvoyant, and psychokinetic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 01-03-2021, 03:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-03T13:03:14-08:00","id":1430907,"title":"","content":"Corr 3/Life 2/Mind 1 isn't a bad selection.<br /> <br /> Life 2 doesn't get to Attribute modification yet, but does allow lower level body manipulations. And it means it's not a huge jump to Life 3 (which is a wonderful thing to have for almost any mage).<br /> <br /> Mind 1 is one of the best level 1 Spheres as you get Mind Shields, and Mental Empowerment (letting you speed up mental actions, multitask them, or boost your Mental Attributes), on top of sensory stuff.<br /> <br /> Though I do think you can do the reality hacker with Entropy 3/Corr 2/Mind 1 effectively as well.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-03T13:22:57-08:00","id":1430910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1430697-optimal-sphere-selection?p=1430907#post1430907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Corr 3/Life 2/Mind 1 isn't a bad selection.<br /> <br /> Life 2 doesn't get to Attribute modification yet, but does allow lower level body manipulations. And it means it's not a huge jump to Life 3 (which is a wonderful thing to have for almost any mage).<br /> <br /> Mind 1 is one of the best level 1 Spheres as you get Mind Shields, and Mental Empowerment (letting you speed up mental actions, multitask them, or boost your Mental Attributes), on top of sensory stuff.<br /> <br /> Though I do think you can do the reality hacker with Entropy 3/Corr 2/Mind 1 effectively as well.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What are your opinions on these two options:<ul><li>Entropy 1, Life 3, Mind 1, Prime 1</li> <li>Correspondence, 1, Entropy 1, Life 3, Mind 1</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-03T15:25:04-08:00","id":1430927,"title":"","content":"They're both solid spreads, though I'm not sure how well they fit the example concept at related.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-03T17:02:13-08:00","id":1430933,"title":"","content":"The justification was to have more analysis capabilities pertaining to the simulation permissions (spheres at 1), and protect the user avatar (as in video game avatar) inside the simulation (Life 3).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 01-03-2021, 08:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-03T17:09:14-08:00","id":1430935,"title":"","content":"I mean, the maximum analysis spread is six 1s. I'm mostly not sure why the focus is on Life 3, as that's the most crude way of protecting the user-avatar. Why increase toughness when you can cause weapons to malfunction or bullets to deflect? Why even be where harm is when you can instantly change location data? Etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-03T17:15:34-08:00","id":1430936,"title":"","content":"Also, remember that self-healing is Life 2. So if you're going for the healing aspect, you don't need the third dot. <br /> <br /> But yeah there are numerous ways to protect yourself that are more effective than making yourself tough and/or self-healing. I forget who said it, but there's a saying to the effect that if you're getting into \u201cfair fights\u201d (where there's doubt about the outcome), you're doing it wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-03T17:17:18-08:00","id":1430938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1430697-optimal-sphere-selection?p=1430935#post1430935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, the maximum analysis spread is six 1s. I'm mostly not sure why the focus is on Life 3, as that's the most crude way of protecting the user-avatar. Why increase toughness when you can cause weapons to malfunction or bullets to deflect? Why even be where harm is when you can instantly change location data? Etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Health restoration, increasing attributes permanently (very important for the character as she can be healthier, better looking, and without impediments like eyesight issues). But I hear recommendations in the spread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-03T18:15:56-08:00","id":1430940,"title":"","content":"Permanent Attribute increases still take XP, even if the rules reduce the cost for raising them if you use magic that can do so.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, you're starting with 6 dots, and you're going to want more because I don't think I've ever seen someone have all the Spheres they'd want for their concept at start.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-03T21:18:43-08:00","id":1430953,"title":"","content":"Aren't optimal spheres about what kind of game/campaign your PC is in and how you want to play them? A streetwise grifter type would do well with Mind 2, Prime 2, and Entropy 2. They'd be a mind reading luck twister. A Stormwarder with the Five point merit ( a character with the ability to cross to the Urmbra unscathed and take those with them safely) would be well served by Spirit 3 and Prime 3. A PC with the right blend of Life and Prime is a healer. A traveler with Correspondence 3 can see the world. Either Mind 3 to understand people, or Entropy 3 to have luck at your beck and call, will help you survive the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 01-04-2021, 03:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-04T04:37:09-08:00","id":1430974,"title":"","content":"Optimal characters in videogames often aren't those that are good at everything, but rather those that excel at some kind of activity. That's why you have roles like &quot;the tank&quot;, &quot;the healer&quot;, &quot;DPS&quot; - Under that logic, probably the best way to protect your user-avatar it's to chose a set of things you want to excel at, and co-op with people that can compliment your weaknesses","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-04T19:30:23-08:00","id":1431109,"title":"","content":"So, what do you think would be more potent, and in tune with the character:<ul><li>Correspondence 3, Entropy 1, Mind 1, Prime 1</li> <li>Correspondence 3, Mind 3</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <br /> I just got tempted by the traveller concept exposed by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar857_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"857\" data-vbnamecard=\"857\">Astromancer</a> but also what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> said about fighting fair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 01-05-2021, 01:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-04T21:58:14-08:00","id":1431116,"title":"","content":"I'd personally take the 3/1/1/1 spread... those are basically the three best level 1 picks for raw utility. Mind 3 is good, and does a lot of potent things, but Corr 3 should be enough to keep your PC safe while you raise other things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-08T20:28:24-07:00","id":1459399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1430697-optimal-sphere-selection?p=1431116#post1431116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd personally take the 3/1/1/1 spread... those are basically the three best level 1 picks for raw utility. Mind 3 is good, and does a lot of potent things, but Corr 3 should be enough to keep your PC safe while you raise other things.</div> </div> </div> </div>A bit of Necromancy on this thread, but it became suddenly relevant in a game, I specially trust <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> opinion since I read <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1207886-character-creation-and-progression-what-is-optimal-what-s-a-trap?p=1208226#post1208226\">a post of his</a>.<br /> <br /> Taking into account what I posted of the character on this thread, and if Entropy is the Affinity sphere, what spread would be better? : <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Correspondence 3, Entropy 1, Mind 1, Prime 1</li> <li>Correspondence 2, Entropy 1, Mind 1, Prime 2</li> <li>Correspondence 3, Entropy 2, Mind 1</li> <li>Entropy 3, Mind 3</li> </ol><br /> I like the last option the most as nearly everything could be coincidental, Entropy and Mind are almost always useful (very versatile), and because two well-picked higher level spheres are orders-of-magnitude better than several at lower levels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-09T06:47:39-07:00","id":1459423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1430697-optimal-sphere-selection?p=1430801#post1430801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I do not understand the fascination with Wonder creation for an starting character, if I read the book right: &amp;quot;<i>In order to craft a wonder, the character must have all of the necessary Spheres</i>.&amp;quot;, so what good is being able to craft it without many other spheres to create something?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because free casting is a newbie trap. Rituals and Artifacts are the main effective ways to cast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-09T09:13:22-07:00","id":1459442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1430697-optimal-sphere-selection?p=1459399#post1459399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A bit of Necromancy on this thread, but it became suddenly relevant in a game, I specially trust <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> opinion since I read <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1207886-character-creation-and-progression-what-is-optimal-what-s-a-trap?p=1208226#post1208226\">a post of his</a>.<br /> <br /> Taking into account what I posted of the character on this thread, and if Entropy is the Affinity sphere, what spread would be better? :<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Correspondence 3, Entropy 1, Mind 1, Prime 1</li> <li>Correspondence 2, Entropy 1, Mind 1, Prime 2</li> <li>Correspondence 3, Entropy 2, Mind 1</li> <li>Entropy 3, Mind 3</li> </ol><br /> I like the last option the most as nearly everything could be coincidental, Entropy and Mind are almost always useful (very versatile), and because two well-picked higher level spheres are orders-of-magnitude better than several at lower levels.</div> </div> </div> </div>Either 1, 2 or 4, depending on your plans for that Correspondence.<br /> <br /> Up to 3 Correspondence is a very good and useful Sphere, as Heavy Arms noted in that post. 3 is where it starts to be Vulgar with some frequency, but still very useful in general (4 is where it really starts to be niche).<br /> <br /> The options where you get a 2 are only good if you plan to never raise that Sphere up from 2 at all, so option 2 may pay off if you really want Correspondence and Prime at 2 and never look back. It isn't a bad choice depending on your goal. Putting your Affinity Sphere at 2 is a no-no.<br /> <br /> You already stated the benefits of option 4, it is a great option and is XP-Optimal. But you need to think how much you want to wait for the effects of the other Spheres. As good as they are, Entropy and Mind won't do everything and if this character really needs Correspondence and/or Prime they won't make it.<br /> <br /> Particularly, your 4 picks are the best &quot;level 1's&quot; in the game anyway, Spheres that give a lot back for just that 1 dot, so options 1 and 2 are strong starting builds right off the bat.<br /> <br /> Caveat: despite what Heavy Arms wrote, if your ST is really, really into Umbra and Spirits and WtA cosmology, Spirit may go from circumstantial all the way up to most important Sphere. It isn't common, but is something to keep in mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-14T15:45:27-07:00","id":1459970,"title":"","content":"Okay so for optimal spheres at an overall level you need to find out which spheres are at an overall level the most useful.<br /> <br /> Personally I place Entropy as the most powerful sphere at an overall level considering some of the bullshit it can do. (Namely: -3 difficulty to all actions, +3 difficulty on opponents actions, apparently heal aggravated damage at level 4, inflict unsoakable aggravated damage at level 4, reduce dicepools of enemies at level 5... ALL dicepools, including Arete, and possibly buff dicepools?) So starting with Entropy 3 is basically a must.<br /> <br /> For another sphere at level 3 I have a few suggestions: Spirit is useful to some degree, fetishes and talens are very powerful, but if you're looking for spies and allies in the umbra spirit is a must. And at level 5 being able to Gilgul another mage is very useful to ensure they stay down. <br /> <br /> Another great option in my opinion is either Correspondence or Life. Life allows you to improve your attributes which is a great bonus to dicepools, especially if Entropy can't boost dicepools (it's ambiguous at best). Being able to attack, teleport, and alter space at range is... to be fair... the best defensive ability possible. You can see anyone coming at any range, use magick on them at any range, and teleport out of a dangerous situation if you need to. There literally isn't a downside. <br /> <br /> Mind is a very useful ability, however true mind control only comes at the 4th dot, and typically has very high difficulties upwards of IIRC willpower +6 or +8 according to How Do You Do That? However if you pull it off, it's wonderfully powerful. Just beware those with Iron Will. <br /> <br /> Personally the only trap sphere in my opinion is Forces. <br /> <br /> If I was to give the best sphere selection choices I'd go for Correspondence 3 / Entropy 3<br /> <br /> And over time investing into Mind / Life","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26413-thatonekiasyd","name":"ThatOneKiasyd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26413_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-15T02:25:16-07:00","id":1460012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ThatOneKiasyd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1430697-optimal-sphere-selection?p=1459970#post1459970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So starting with Entropy 3 is basically a must.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that that depends on your ST, a player continually blagging things with entropy could quickly become a pain in the posterior, and be likely to get penalised. I can't find it but I'm sure there's a sidebar or paragraph somewhere in the M20 book that talks about sequences of excessively lucky things rapidly becoming vulgar with the consequential paradox or backlash of that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}